# Rights Database — SYS$SYSTEM:RIGHTSLIST.DAT
#
# THE VALUES IN THIS FILE ARE MEASURED, NOT CHOSEN (vms-2f8).
# Oracle: OpenVMS VAX V7.3, lab node VAX1, 2026-08-05. Full transcript,
# including the AUTHORIZE SHOW/IDENTIFIER/FULL listing these rows come from,
# is docs/oracle/vax73-rights-database.md.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE USED TO SAY, AND WHY IT WAS WRONG.
# It shipped five rows -- INTERACTIVE:1 BATCH:2 NETWORK:3 LOCAL:4 REMOTE:5 --
# and nothing read it. Asked of real VMS, NONE of the values 1..5 is an
# identifier at all; every one answers the null string:
#
#     F$IDENTIFIER(1,"NUMBER_TO_NAME")  ->  ""     ... through 5, all ""
#     F$IDENTIFIER("LOCAL","NAME_TO_NUMBER") -> -2147483644 = %X80000004
#
# The numbering was an invention, and the ordering was too: the real
# environmental identifiers are %X80000001..%X80000006 assigned ALPHABETICALLY
# (BATCH, DIALUP, INTERACTIVE, LOCAL, NETWORK, REMOTE). DIALUP was missing
# entirely. The Attributes column was RESOURCE on all five rows; on real VMS
# these identifiers carry NO attributes.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT — an OVMX design choice, deliberately labelled as one (Rule 8).
#
#     IDENTIFIER:VALUE:ATTRIBUTES
#
# Real RIGHTSLIST.DAT is an indexed RMS file. Nothing in this project has
# observed its bytes, so OVMX defines its own text representation rather than
# guessing at VSI's. It is NOT presented as VMS-authentic.
#
# VALUE is written in the notation AUTHORIZE prints for that kind of
# identifier, so a row here reads the same as the row the tool shows:
#     %Xnnnnnnnn   general identifier (hexadecimal)
#     [g,m]        UIC identifier (OCTAL, as every VMS UIC is written -- vms-e60)
#
# ATTRIBUTES is a comma-separated KGB$M_ list (see src/libvms/include/kgbdef.h)
# and is EMPTY for every row below, because it is empty on the oracle.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY.
#
# 1. NO UIC IDENTIFIERS. The oracle's listing has one UIC identifier per UAF
#    account (SYSTEM [1,4], DEFAULT [200,200], ...), because on VMS AUTHORIZE
#    maintains the account and its identifier together. OVMX has no such
#    coupled path, so shipping those rows HERE as well as in SYSUAF.DAT would
#    be two files free to disagree about one account's UIC -- which is exactly
#    the defect vms-e60 just closed (LOGINOUT stamping one UIC while
#    F$IDENTIFIER answered another). UIC identifiers are therefore DERIVED
#    from SYSUAF.DAT at lookup time; see src/libvms/rtl/rightslist.c. One
#    source, by construction.
#
# 2. NO DECWINDOWS / VMS$BUFFER_OBJECT_USER / VMS$MEM_RESIDENT_USER. The
#    oracle carries them; they name facilities OVMX does not have. Observing
#    that VMS ships an identifier is not authority for OVMX to ship one for a
#    facility that cannot grant or check it (Rule 10 -- match it or hide it,
#    never invent the plausible-looking middle).
#
# 3. NO SITE ROWS. BARON, SYS$NODE_VAX*, TCPIP$*, SECSRV$*, MAIL$SERVER and
#    the rest of the oracle's listing belong to that lab, not to VMS.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
BATCH:%X80000001:
DIALUP:%X80000002:
INTERACTIVE:%X80000003:
LOCAL:%X80000004:
NETWORK:%X80000005:
REMOTE:%X80000006:
